MAJOR_VERSION=5
STANDARD_VERSION=3
RELEASE_VERSION=0
PRERELEASE=1
DEV_VERSION=8
DESCRIPTION=AI tooling: reuse before you implement, plus the DevOps team skill. AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md gain a Reuse before you implement section (research existing drivers, helpers and contracts in depth before writing new code, never two functions that do the same thing, extend instead of copying, add one shared helper and point every caller at it), mirrored for Cursor in .cursor/rules/reuse_before_implement.mdc. The devops-multi-agent-team skill from Homework Central is imported under .cursor/skills, .cursor/agents and .cursor/commands (goal, code-review, repro, triage, create-subagent), adapted to this repo: its Researcher writes a reuse map before a Coder starts, its Reviewers block duplicated new code, its CodeQL policy covers C and C++, and this repo's versioning and driver-boundary rules take precedence. .cursor/thoughts is git-ignored except its keepfile. First use (issue 384, D1): one shared hex codec, kernel/include/fl/hex.h (fl_hex_nibble, fl_hex_encode, fl_hex_decode, header-only), replaces the copies in user_db.c, bridge.c, kq_delivery.c and password_hash.cpp with identical output (checked against the old build with a fixed-salt password hash); new make test_hex. Rules: one .ver per PR, added with the first real push after QA and Security approval and only edited afterwards; the DevOps skill staffs 2 to 3 subagents per function and moves idle seats to busy ones. Not covered: Buildkite, Linear, Sonar, Snyk, Composio and Mainframe are named by the skill but optional here, and no CodeQL workflow exists in this repo yet. Items 2 and 3 (D2, D3): fl_fs_read_file in server_shared_fs.c (one open, fstat, regular files only, size cap, no truncated read, wipe on failure) replaces read_all, the letter-store reader and the lab reader, and header-only fl_fs_basename in kernel/include/fl/path.h replaces the strrchr copies in kq_checkpoint.c, lab_kq.c, net_file_delivery.c, fs_provider.c and fat32_host_files.c; new make test_fs_helpers. Differences: a directory, FIFO or device now gives a generic error, a file that changes during the read fails instead of truncating, the lab reader is capped at FL_KQ_LETTER_MAX, and a NULL path gives an error or an empty name instead of a crash. QA now ends with a bug hunt instead of CodeQL, and Coders send questions to standing Review, Security and QA seats. The wasm lab build was not compiled here (no emcc). Item 4 (D4): one shared fl_random_bytes in kernel/include/fl/random.h (getrandom loop, /dev/urandom fallback restricted to the real urandom device, getentropy under Emscripten; all or nothing, zeroed buffer and errno on failure, no weak fallback) replaces the /dev/urandom reads, the RAND_bytes uses and the time-seeded or xorshift values in password_hash.cpp, bridge.c, kq_checkpoint.c, net_wifi_crypto.c, server_shared_digest.c, net_dns.c and net_macvlan.c; DNS and DHCP now fail closed when no entropy is available; fl_hex_decode rejects lengths that would wrap; new make test_random and check-weak-rng. Security runs a SOC 2 review on every change and CodeQL is dropped from the DevOps skill. Untested: the entropy-failure branches have no committed test (QA demonstrated them with interposition), the wasm and non-Linux paths, and live DNS and DHCP. Item 5 (D5), a security fix: a delivered file name that is not a plain name (a path separator, '.' or '..', a control byte, an embedded NUL, 128 bytes or more, or a reserved suffix .part .meta .kqtf .kqseen .kqbak in any case) is now refused at the offer decode, the catalog register paths, save_offer, the landing name choice and the overwrite destination leaf, where before a remote sender could place a file outside the landing directory; landings go through the destination directory handle (openat, no link following, .part created exclusively, quarantine gate on the normalised path) and new files are 0600; fl_fs_name_is_plain in fl/path.h, fl_server_shared_name_is_reserved and fl_server_shared_resolve_local_path in server_shared_fs.c. Differences: '.' and '..' are refused instead of renamed, 127-byte names cannot take a ' (n)' variant, overwrite names must be under 128 bytes, KeyQuorum deliveries can no longer carry a .meta name, a missing landing directory fails the landing. Untested or open: the wasm and non-Linux paths, the channel sidecar NUL check has no test of its own. Other hex copies remain in server_shared_digest.c, net_wifi_db.c, disk.c, cluster.c, commands.c and lab_kq.c. Item 5 follow-up (D5): an overwrite now replaces the file atomically through the directory handle (a failed write keeps the original, a hard-linked leaf is replaced instead of written through, a read-only, link, directory or FIFO leaf is refused, an overwritten file is always 0600 and loses its old owner, ACL and extended attributes, staging removes an existing <leaf>.part, and the directory must be writable); the offer-decode test no longer uses memmem. Item 16 (D16): fl_kq_cp_for_each_event in kq_checkpoint.c walks the history lines for both server file log (shell) and fl_lab_kq_log; a trailing fragment without a newline is still skipped. Item 10 (D10): fl_user_db_secret_matches in user_db.c is the one derive-and-compare (asm_mem_ct_equal, derived public wiped on every exit); fl_user_db_open_key and open_box share one body that securely zeroes the secret on every failure after the open (open_key used a plain zero before); bridge.c secret_is_for is gone; password_hash.cpp compares the stored digest as raw bytes in constant time and wipes its digests and the legacy salt-and-password copy; difference: stored password hashes in upper-case hex now verify (they never matched before; nothing writes them); password_hash.o now needs the mem_asm objects (test_wifi_db link fixed); new make test_secret_compare. Item 12 (D12): the KeyQuorum driver is registered by fl_driver_registry_register_all with a synthetic keyquorum device when built with -DFL_WITH_KEYQUORUM (Makefile CFLAGS; run make clean once after pulling), the shell-start registration is gone, and fl_kq_driver_get is unchanged: resolving through the registry waits for D11 and must compare with fl_kq_driver_desc and re-probe the ABI; new make test_drivers_no_keyquorum. Untested or open: the wasm lab, ARM, bare-metal and vm-sdl builds were not run here, concurrent overwrites of one leaf can return an error where the old write interleaved content, drivers_init called repeatedly without a shutdown grows the registry, and D6 (commit_all move) is deferred as it is not a small change. Item 6 (D6): fl_fs_commit_files in server_shared_fs.c is the one all-or-nothing replace of up to four files (each existing file is kept as <name>.kqbak, the staged parts are renamed in, a failed rename puts the replaced files back and removes ones that did not exist, a copy fallback runs where hard links are missing) and replaces commit_all in kq_checkpoint.c; the landing helpers moved with it, join_path in server_shared_db.c is gone in favour of fl_fs_join_path, FL_FS_BACKUP_SUFFIX is defined once, and names over 244 bytes, duplicate names, a name that is another name plus .part or .kqbak, and a failing existence check are refused before anything is written. Known limit, a named follow-up: if the restore rename itself fails the .kqbak is still removed, which needs its own design. Review-bot rule: feedback from CodeRabbit or Codex is verified against the code, resolved by a Coder who did not write the code under comment and reviewed by an independent Reviewer; a fix outside the listed exceptions needs no separate Security or QA pass because the Actions run builds and tests, this repository has no security scan so the exceptions cover sensitive code, rule files and CI paths, and the version_def.h exception requires the bot author, committer and subject plus a header equal to the generator output. Seats are identified by a <role>-<hex> hash id, not a letter. Not covered: the wasm lab and the non-openat path were not run here.
